ion when required |", "| changes_requested | in_progress, blocked | Bounded repair scope and new attempt |", "| accepted | done, changes_requested | Coordinator verifies every criterion, evidence and required owner decisions |", "| blocked | planned | New evidence resolves recorded blocker; reevaluate readiness, never jump to done |", "| done | planned | Explicit reopening reason; prior acceptance preserved in event history |", "", "`ready` is explicit and checked, not inferred from file existence. `next` prints the first", "ready task in queue order. At most one task is in_progress/review/changes_requested/accepted.", "`done` means its lasting deliverables, tests, independent review and applicable human", "acceptance are complete. `blocked` records missing fact, failed assumption or unavailable", "input, impact, smallest resolution action, and owner. Source gaps can be valid importer", "outputs while still blocking later gameplay; do not mark import blocked for every missing PDF.", "", "Use `transition --task ID --to STATE --evidence PATH`. Evidence is JSON with `role`,", "`actor`, `summary`, `criteria`, `artifacts`, `model`, `reasoning`, `configuration_evidence`,", "and optional `semantic_decision`. Unknown measured configuration is null with a reason.", "For delivery/review/acceptance also supply `checks`, a nonempty list of command and", "exit_code records. All required checks must have exit code zero. In-progress claims", "require confirmed `model: gpt-6.1-sol` and `reasoning: high`; unknown configuration", "is recorded as a blocker until the operator confirms the actual session settings.", "The command checks structural gates and file hashes, not the truth or authority of a", "human statement. Evidence is append-only by hash in queue events; changes invalidate checks.", "See [evidence shapes](EVIDENCE.md) for a checkpoint/delivery example. Executor status", "updates go through the transition command; the coordinator owns structural queue edits.", "For a semantic task, accepted requires a human decision artifact from the owner or a", "documented authorized reviewer. Do not fabricate one. Routine technical acceptance can", "be recorded by the coordinator after independent review without another owner confirmation.", "", "## One task cycle", "", "1. Coordinator validates queue and chooses `next`. Resolve `refine` before readiness.", "2. Generate a packet with exact allowed context. Binary source references are hashed,", "   not dumped into text; read only pages/IDs named by the task. External WGU context is", "   explicitly scoped in the card, never scanned through historical manifests.", "3. Operator starts the selected executor manually using [the launch prompt](PROMPTS.md).", "   Confirm Sol/high from UI/session metadata; requested settings are not evidence.", "4. Record claim and checkpoint; implement only this increment; record changed files,", "   checks, measured usage and unresolved assumptions. Preserve unrelated working changes.", "5. Freeze delivery hashes and enter review. Operator supplies the review prompt to a", "   separate reviewer. Evaluate source meaning separately from code mechanics.", "6. Repair scoped findings, rerun affected checks and obtain a new review of changed hashes.", "7. Coordinator records acceptance then done, renders views, makes the next eligible task", "   ready, and prepares a new handoff. Do not start the next task just to finish this one.", "", "## Refinement and corpus partitioning", "", "`refine` tasks are not executable until exact prerequisites/paths/cases are pinned. Edit", "the record to `implementation` or `content` after refinement; keep the decision in events.", "For a corpus task, create bounded child records with explicit target IDs, context-only", "IDs, source hashes/pages and disjoint output paths. The parent becomes a closure task"], "truncated": true}

